\section{Introduction}
Whitesands (also called East Tanna or Narak; ISO 639-3 tnp) is an Oceanic language spoken on the eastern coast of Tanna, Vanuatu. It is closely related to North Tanna and Lenakel. Little published educational material turned up in search. Kwamera (Nafe) is a different language, and its materials are not listed here.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
The PARADISEC collection of Jeremy Hammond's 2008 Whitesands documentation is reported to include a Whitesands--French school word list and storybooks. I did not open the items, so contents and access conditions are unverified.
\begin{itemize}
\item PARADISEC item: \url{https://catalog.paradisec.org.au/repository/JHWS1/20080503}
\end{itemize}

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia overview of the language: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whitesands_language}
\item Jeremy Hammond (2009), master's thesis on the grammar of nouns and verbs in Whitesands. It is cited in the search summary and Wikipedia, but I did not see a direct download URL.
\item Numeral data: \url{https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Whitesands.htm}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
No Whitesands scripture or community organisation was found in the search results.

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item PARADISEC collection with Capell recordings from East Tanna, where Whitesands is the main language: \url{https://catalog.paradisec.org.au/repository/AC1/LT9}
\item Cambridge Language Centre page on Tanna languages (contents not verified): \url{https://www.langcen.cam.ac.uk/resources/langt/tanna.html}
\end{itemize}

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
No Whitesands dictionary, textbook or curriculum was found. A curriculum would have to start from the Hammond documentation, the PARADISEC materials and work with the community. This dossier is short because little was found.
\end{document}
